$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Reactions of diazonium salts with KBr. General
procedure. To a dispersion of 238 mg (2 mmol) of finely ground KBr in 1
ml of dry MeCN was added at stirring 36 mg (0.1 mmol, 10 mol%) of
dibenzo-18-crown-6, 14 mg (0.1 mmol, 10 mol%) of CuBr, and 22 mg (0.1
mmol, 10 мол%) of CuBr2. After stirring for 2 min 11.6 mg (0.1 mmol, 10
mol%) of TMEDA was added. After 30 min of stirring was added dropwise a
solution of 1 mmol of diazonium salt I in 1 ml of dry MeCN, the obtained
mixture was stirred for 1 h at room temperature and poured into 50 ml of
ethyl ether and passed through celite to remove the inorganic salts. On
evaporating the solvent in a vacuum we obtained the corresponding pure
aryl bromide IV. (IVj), yield 90%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Sandmeyer reaction, alternatively reaction carried out using
1,10-phenanthroline as ligand instead of tetramethylethylenediamine gave
97% yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Cu(I)/Cu(II)/TMEDA, new effective available catalyst of Sandmeyer
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sigeev, A. S.; Beletskaya, I. P.; Petrovskii, P. V.; Peregudov, A. S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of Organic Chemistry (2012), 48(8), 1055-1058

