$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
fluoro[2.2]paracyclophane 3a-c. Optically pure 1a-c (0.50 mmol) was
separately added to a stirred solution of 40% HBF4 (0.25 mL, 1.50 mmol)
in ethanol (0.50 mL). The mixture was purged with nitrogen and then
heated to 60 °C, under nitrogen bubbling, until a clear solution was
resulted. After 10 min, the solution was cooled at -5 °C, and then
isoamyl nitrite (0.20 mL, 1.50 mmol) was added dropwise. The temperature
was kept at -5 °C, and stirring was continued for another 1 h. Diethyl
ether (2.0 mL) was added, and then the resulting precipitate was
filtered, washed with diethyl ether (2.0 mL), and finally dried under
vacuum to obtain the diazonium fluoroborate which was used without
further purification (2a: 169 mg, yield 85%; 2b; 2c: 146 mg, yield 91%).
(Rp)-4-bromo-12-fluoro[2.2]paracyclophane (3b): White solid. Yield: 103
mg (85%). Mp:152-154 °C; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.03 - 6.93 (m, 1H),
6.66 (dd, J = 11.5, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 6.58 - 6.31 (m, 4H), 3.53 - 3.29 (m,
2H), 3.15 - 2.90 (m, 4H), 2.81 (ddd, J = 13.1, 10.2, 6.3 Hz, 1H), 2.72 -
2.58 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ(d, J = 245.7 Hz), 142.6 (d, J =
7.4 Hz), 141.4, 137.9, 135.1 (d, J = 6.3 Hz), 134.5, 133.0, 131.4, 129.7,
127.6 (d, J = 2.8 Hz), 126.1, 125.1 (d, J = 17.9 Hz), 117.1 (d, J = 22.6
Hz), 35.0, 32.9, 32.2, 32.2, 29.9.; [α]20 D +86.8 (c 0.5, CH2Cl2); Anal.
Calcd for C16H14BrF: C, 62.97; H, 4.62. Found: C, 62.77; H, 5.01. The
enantiomeric ratio was determined by HPLC analysis on a Chiralpak IA
column, λ = 254 nm, eluent: hexane/iPrOH (150:1), flow rate = 0.5 mL/min;
tR = 10.05 min (Sp), tR = 10.51 min (Rp); er (Rp: Sp = 99.7:0.3).
