$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1. Synthesis of 1,3,5-Br3-2-ClC6H2 (16) A 500 mL, two-necked,
round-bottom flask fitted with a dropping funnel was charged with
2,4,6-tribromoaniline (3.30 g, 10 mmol) and hydrochloric acid (6M, 65
mL). The mixture was stirred on an ice bath for 20 min. Afterwards, to
the suspension, was added drop-wise a solution of sodium nitrite (1.04 g,
15 mmol) in water (50 mL) and the mixture was stirred on the ice bath for
1 h. Copper(I) chloride (2.97 g, 30 mmol) was added in small portions
with vigorous stirring. After the addition ended, the mixture was stirred
for 30 min on an ice bath and 30 min at rt. The mixture was extracted
with diethyl ether (4x15 mL). The organic fractions were combined and
dried over Na2SO4. Filtration and evaporation of the solvent gave 3.21 g
of brown solid. This product was sublimed at 70 °C (4x10-2 mbar) to give
16. Slightly yellow solid, yield 2.49 g, 71 %. Mp 92 - 94 °C (91 °C
lit.);2 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ 7.73 (s, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz):
δ 135.22 (s), 124.14 (s), 120.62 (s).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
