$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reactions of diazonium salts with KCl. General procedure. To a dispersion
of 149 mg (2 mmol) of finely ground KCl in 1 ml of dry MeCN was added at
stirring 0.1 mmol of a phase-transfer catalyst, 9.9 mg (0.1 mmol, 10
mol%) of CuCl, and 13.4 mg (0.1 mmol, 10 mol%) of CuCl2. After that 0.1
mmol (10 mol%) of ligand was added. After 30 min of stirring was added
dropwise a solution of 1 mmol of diazonium salt I in 1-2 ml of dry MeCN,
the obtained mixture was stirred for 1 or 24 h at room temperature or 1 h
at 50°С, the reaction progress was monitored by GLC or 19F NMR
spectroscopy. On the completion of the reaction the reaction mixture was
poured into 50 ml of ethyl ether and passed through celite to remove the
inorganic salts. The solvent was evaporated in a vacuum, and the residue
if necessary was purified by column. chromatography IIa, yield 88%; III,
yield 11%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM phase transfer catalysis, Sandmeyer reaction, optimization study,
optimized on ligand in catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Cu(I)/Cu(II)/TMEDA, new effective available catalyst of Sandmeyer
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sigeev, A. S.; Beletskaya, I. P.; Petrovskii, P. V.; Peregudov, A. S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of Organic Chemistry (2012), 48(8), 1055-1058

